  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SHIFT &#x2013; Scaling-up clean Heating Investments to Facilitate energy Transformation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aimed to transform the heating sector in Monogolia by demonstrating the applicability of renewable energy technologies for district heating systems and supporting the adoption of a clean heating policy and investment plan. The project intended to support Mongolia to achieve its NDC commitment to reduce emissions from energy production by 32% by 2030. The project intended to establish 4 solar district heating (SDH) plants (11 MW each) and mobilise EUR 15 m. of public and private funds. This was expected to lead to a reduction of 2.3 Mt CO2e during the project lifetime and 10 years after the implementation.</narrative>
  </description>
